<h1>Hide All</h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>tree context menu &gt; Hide All</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Hide All</span> <span lang="EN-GB">hides marked entities and groups. See</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../User_Interface/Tree_Context_Menus.htm">Tree Context Menus</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details about marking tree items. This command is grayed if the entity is hidden, or all entities in the group are hidden. If you apply</span> <span class="Command">Hide All</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to the root, all objects in the scene will be hidden. Hiding entities is not stored, i.e. next time when you open the file all entities will be displayed.</span></p>
